```
.\"
.\" THR_EXIT(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH THR_EXIT 2 "January 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
thr_exit \- terminate the calling thread
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/thr.h>
.PP
.BI "void thr_exit(void *" status ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR thr_exit ()
terminates the calling thread. The
.I status
value is made available to any other thread in the same process that
calls
.BR thr_join (2)
for this thread.
.PP
If the thread is the last thread in the process, the process exits
as if
.BR exit (3)
was called with a status of 0.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR thr_exit ()
function does not return.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 456
Arguments:      status (on stack)
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR thr_new (2),
.BR thr_join (2),
.BR pthread_exit (3)
.SH HISTORY
Based on FreeBSD's thr_exit(2) for BSD compatibility.
```
